          },
          "description": "<p></p><p>Core Maintainer of Biopass (Linux Biometric Authentication System) with 150+ stars. It is used by real users and actively maintained as an alternative to existing Linux authentication solutions (e.g., <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" href=\"https://github.com/boltgolt/howdy\">Howdy</a>).</p><ul><li><p>Architected a pluggable authentication system integrating with Linux PAM stack</p></li><li><p>Built biometric authentication workflows (face + fingerprint) with unified UX similar to Windows Hello</p></li><li><p>Implemented IR-based anti-spoofing pipeline with on-device AI inference</p></li><li><p>Designed lightweight runtime (~13MB) with minimal dependencies, significantly smaller than alternatives (e.g., Howdy's size is from 1GB to 2GB, including dependencies)</p></li><li><p>Worked at OS level: login managers, PAM modules, credential propagation</p></li><li><p>Packaged and distributed across APT, RPM, and AUR ecosystems</p></li><li><p>Led project direction, code reviews, and community contributions</p></li></ul><p></p>"
        }
